  "id": "Compound::DB00674 - Gene::55584",
  "verbalization": "Galantamine, a cholinesterase inhibitor, is implicated in the interaction with the acetylcholine-activated Cation-selective Channel Activity, which is mediated through the Chrna9 channel. The evidence suggests that Galantamine binds to Chrng or Chrne, both of which are involved in the same biological process as Chrna9. This binding likely modulates the activity of the channel, potentially affecting the flow of ions across cell membranes, which is critical for neuromuscular function. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible relationship, with Galantamine acting as a modulator of the channel activity that ultimately influences Chrna9. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same target and mechanism supports a unified explanation for the observed interactions.",
